<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB leaves discount rate at 1.00 pct.</title>
<headline>SNB leaves discount rate at 1.00 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank said it had left its discount rate unchanged at 1.00 percent at a regular weekly meeting of its central bank council.</p>
<p>&quot;No change in the discount rate,&quot; an SNB spokesman said in response to an enquiry.</p>
<p>At 1.00 percent, the discount rate matches the historic low maintained from February 1978 to November 1979.</p>
<p>The rate was last changed September 26, 1996 when it was lowered from 1.50 percent.</p>
</text>
